From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Llewellyn-Jones <david@flypig.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 7 Jul 2024 16:23:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 41/67] Disable PipeWire WebRTC capture on SFOS. JB#53756

See the following page for background to this change:
https://firefox-source-docs.mozilla.org/build/buildsystem/gn.html

The old ESR91 patch carried large generated GN configuration snapshots to
remove desktop Linux assumptions from the WebRTC build.  ESR115 no longer
needs those generated files in the downstream patch stack.

Keep the one remaining Sailfish-specific GN change: do not enable PipeWire
desktop capture for SFOS builds.

Co-authored-by: Denis Grigorev <d.grigorev@omprussia.ru>
---
 third_party/libwebrtc/webrtc.gni | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/libwebrtc/webrtc.gni b/third_party/libwebrtc/webrtc.gni
index 92beecc5e4e7..434857178140 100644
--- a/third_party/libwebrtc/webrtc.gni
+++ b/third_party/libwebrtc/webrtc.gni
@@ -149,7 +149,7 @@ declare_args() {
   # By default it's only enabled on desktop Linux (excludes ChromeOS) and
   # only when using the sysroot as PipeWire is not available in older and
   # supported Ubuntu and Debian distributions.
-  rtc_use_pipewire = is_linux && use_sysroot
+  rtc_use_pipewire = is_linux && use_sysroot && !is_sfos
 
   # Set this to link PipeWire and required libraries directly instead of using the dlopen.
   rtc_link_pipewire = false
